    "reviewStatus": "claude-drafted",
    "note": "Thresholds are a domain judgment call pending review against FACSI's actual filter sets (K-3, instruments/objectives/lines/detectors, not yet authored). Emission proximity is the primary (error-severity) check: typical bandpass emission filters are 20-40 nm wide and most dye/FP emission curves have a 40-60 nm FWHM, so peaks this close will substantially co-register in each other's detection window regardless of exact filter choice. Excitation proximity is secondary (warning-severity): standard laser lines are spaced 40-100+ nm apart specifically so one line excites one dye class, and this flag makes the existing confocal-sequential-scanning advisor tip panel-specific and concrete."
